    "error_patterns": {
      "A_confident_false_self_serve": {
        "apps": [
          "Brex",
          "Gladly"
        ],
        "description": "Enterprise, sales-led products with NO free signup were graded self_serve/ready because their docs describe generating an API token inside the product UI. The LLM conflates 'existing customer can mint a token in Settings' with 'anyone can sign up free.' Highest-stakes error: a false green light on apps that block you at the door."
      },
      "B_partial_unknown_is_a_blind_spot": {
        "apps": [
          "Smartsheet",
          "Neo4j",
          "Podio",
          "SE Ranking",
          "Salesforce Commerce Cloud",
          "Google Ads"
        ],
        "description": "Every 'partial/unknown' in the sample was actually determinable. 4 were truly self_serve/ready (under-sold) and 2 were truly gated/blocked (under-flagged). Root cause: the fetched auth/reference page rarely states the signup/pricing model, so the model returns 'unknown', which collapses to 'partial'. 'partial' is functioning as a 'did not check the pricing/signup page' bucket, not a real middle verdict."
      }
    },
    "bias_direction": "Two-sided, but the dangerous side is Pattern A: gated enterprise products mislabeled self_serve/ready (2/2 enterprise-sales apps in the sample). Pattern B mostly under-sells genuinely self-serve apps and hides a couple of gates behind 'partial'.",
    "publish_recommendation": "NOT publish-ready. 60% on the two highest-stakes fields, with 2 confident false 'ready' verdicts on gated products, means it needs another pass that checks the actual pricing/signup page (is there a free/instant tier?) rather than only the API auth docs, and that re-resolves every 'partial/unknown' instead of treating it as final."
  },
